# Pin line endings so Windows checkouts don't produce phantom
# "modified" files from CRLF/LF drift. All text files are stored
# as LF in the repo AND kept as LF in the working tree, regardless
# of the local `core.autocrlf` setting. This matches CI (Linux)
# behavior and Biome's format-check expectations.
#
# Without this, Windows users with `core.autocrlf=true` see 20+
# unrelated files show as modified on every `git status`, because
# git thinks it will convert LF→CRLF on next checkout even though
# working-tree content is unchanged.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats — never touch line endings.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
